==Differences between the movie and the manga==
* In the manga, {{Ash}} travels alone without {{ashfr}}.
* [[Levi]] and [[Cherie]] don't appear in the manga, with their roles replaced by several unnamed assistants to [[Alva]]. Therefore, only {{me|Alakazam}}, Mega {{p|Glalie}}, Mega {{p|Tyranitar}}, Mega {{p|Beedrill}}, Mega {{p|Manectric}}, and Mega {{p|Banette}} appear in the manga, under control of Alva, along with his Mega {{p|Gengar}}.
* Alva's staff has three Mega Wave jewels instead of one.
* [[Kimia]] and [[Raleigh]] don't appear in the manga. Without Kimia's vehicles, Ash has to travel on {{OBP|Volcanion|M19}}'s back, and later, with a jetpack.
* {{TRT}} doesn't appear at all, making it the first time they haven't appeared in the manga adaptation of a movie.
* There are two [[Pokémon hunter]]s, instead of one like in the movie. One of them also uses Kimia's flying gear from the movie.
* {{OBP|Magearna|M19}} actively fights to protect the [[Nebel Plateau]], before surrendering itself to Alva.
* The structure of the flying fortress's interior is completely different in the manga.
* Ash doesn't use any Pokémon other than {{AP|Pikachu}}. This leads to a climax battle of two against seven.
* As [[Squishy]] is not in the manga, Nebel Plateau is protected from the destructive beam by the combined effort of all Pokémon in the Nebel Plateau.
* At the end of the manga, Alva was arrested by [[Officer Jenny]] instead of Kimia.

